+## Sales import and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO 8601 instant with a zone,
+`qty` a whole number above zero) and answers
+`{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`: the tickets imported and the dishes sold on
+them (the sum of `qty`). Tickets imported earlier are skipped and not
+counted. The file is all or nothing: an invalid row answers `bad_request`
+and an item running out answers `sale_not_enough_stock`; both messages name
+the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one line per
+item with use in those days (inclusive, UTC):
+`{ "itemId", "name", "unit", "theoretical", "actual", "difference" }`, where
+`difference` is `actual - theoretical`.
